  "raw": {
    "https://www.lindsey.edu/about-lwc/Offices-and-Services/Human-Resources/job-opportunities.cfm": {
      "title": "Employment Opportunities",
      "description": "Job Opportunities RAIDERPORTAL Offices and Services About LWU Admissions Academics Athletics Alumni Campus Life LWU Virtual Campus Tour About LWU Home Mission Accreditations Board of Trustees History John B. Begley Chapel Employment Opportunities Campus Map/Directions Parking Campus Safety About the Region Civic Engagement Career Services Veteran Services Cranmer Dining Center Holloway Wellness Center Media Relations Factbook Academics Home Academic Excellence Registrar's Office Academic Affairs Academic Schools Academic Calendar Course Offerings Academic Catalog Student Success Center Library Writing Center Teaching & Learning Commons Special Academic Opportunities Undergraduate Degrees Graduate Degrees Campus Locations Admissions Home Visit LWU LWU Virtual Campus Tour Viewbook Undergraduate Graduate LWU Online Orientation Days Transfer Postgraduate International Students Extended Campuses Veteran Services Meet Your Counselor Tuition and Fees Financial Aid Scholarships Campus Map FAQ Apply Now Schedule A Visit Request Info Make a Gift Alumni Home Alumni Council Career Services Church Relations Cornerstone Events President's Annual Report Success After LWU Update Information Ways To Give Make A Gift Social Connections Athletics Home Master Schedule Athletic Staff Mission Statement Quick Facts NAIA Mid-South Conference USA Cycling Southeast Collegiate Cycling Conference U.S. Bowling Congress LWU Sports Network News Archive Campus Life Home Virtual Student Activities Office of Student Services Residence Life Holloway Health and Wellness Center Campus Map Dining Services Student Organizations Spiritual Life Student Activities International Student Programs (ISP) International Students Handbook RaiderBucks Safety & Security Counseling Services Green Dot Student Handbook Title IX Blue Raider Sports Medicine Lindsey Wilson University RaiderPortal Home About LWU Admissions Academics Athletics Alumni Campus Life Lindsey Wilson University 210 Lindsey Wilson Street Columbia, Kentucky 42728 800-264-0138 • 270-384-2126 Employment Opportunities Equal Employment Opportunity Act It is the policy of Lindsey Wilson University to assure equal employment opportunity for all employees and candidates for employment. The employment practices of Lindsey Wilson University are to recruit, hire, and promote individuals on the basis of qualifications, ability, past performance, and other job-related measures. Such matters as race, color, sex, age, natural origin, religious beliefs, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, disability, genetic information, marital status, amnesty, status as a covered veteran, and any other characteristic protected by law, are not factors in consideration of qualifications. This policy applies as well to the areas of compensation, benefits, education, University-sponsored training, layoffs, opportunities for advancement, termination, recall, transfer, leaves of absence, and all other privileges and conditions of employment. All recruitment efforts, including employment advertising, are set forth in a manner making it clear that all individuals are welcome to apply without regard to any characteristic protected by law. As an equal opportunity employer, Lindsey Wilson University intends to comply with applicable laws and executive orders. All employees are expected to conduct themselves in accordance with this policy. Any employee with questions or concerns about any type of discrimination in the workplace should bring the matter to the attention of their immediate supervisor, Human Resources, any Vice President, or the President. Any employee who makes a report of discrimination will not be discriminated or retaliated against by reason of having made the report.  Acts of discrimination by managers, supervisors, and other employees, including sexual and racial harassment, are not tolerated and will result in disciplinary action. To apply online, please complete the Employment Application. CARPENTER Posted: 9/04/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking an energetic individual to assume carpenter duties. Selected applicants must enjoy working with young adults, faculty and staff in a living/learning environment. The Carpenter will be responsible for a wide range of carpentry tasks including installation, repair, and maintenance of various structures and fixtures across campus. This position plays a crucial role in ensuring the safety, functionality, and aesthetic appeal of our facilities. High school diploma or equivalent required.  Vocational or technical training in carpentry is preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. APPRENTICE CARPENTER Posted: 9/04/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking an energetic individual to assume Apprentice Carpenter duties. Selected applicants must enjoy working with young adults, faculty and staff in a living/learning environment. The Carpenter will be responsible for a wide range of carpentry tasks including installation, repair, and maintenance of various structures and fixtures across campus. This position plays a crucial role in ensuring the safety, functionality, and aesthetic appeal of our facilities. High school diploma or equivalent required. Vocational or technical training in carpentry is preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. FINANCIAL AID ASSOCIATE Posted: 9/03/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking candidates for a Financial Aid Associate. The Financial Aid Associate is the first point of contact for visitors and students. This person will answer general financial aid questions through phone, email, and in person. Financial aid associate will assist in keeping the office organized and ensuring that operations run smoothly. Other clerical duties will be assigned as needed. A bachelor’s degree is required, and two years of higher education or customer service experience preferred. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. DIRECTOR OF STUDENT ACTIVITIES & SPECIAL EVENTS COORDINATOR Posted: 9/02/2026 The position directs and oversees the development and organization of extracurricular and co-curricular activities to the Student population of Lindsey Wilson. Promotes student morale, collaborates with other offices, and works with community agencies as well as campus clubs and organizations, often working closely with visiting groups on campus. In keeping with Lindsey Wilson’s Mission, Student Activities offers opportunities for students to grow and develop every day through events and activities. The duties and responsibilities for this position include the following. Develop and implement extracurricular and co-curricular activities for the student population of Lindsey Wilson Coordinates events, meetings, conferences, summer camps, and weddings, including but not limited to Opening Weekend, Malvina Farkle Day, Parents Weekend, Homecoming, and Spring Formal. Budget manager of the Student Activities accounts Other duties as assigned. Bachelor's Degree is required, and p referred event planning experience To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. RESIDENT DIRECTOR Posted:  8/31/2026 The Resident Director is a full-time, 12 month live-in professional staff member with the Residence Life Department. Within Residence Life, this position focuses on enhancing the quality of life of students in the assigned residential area, fostering community, being attentive to safety and security of residents and assisting with facility operations. This position will work daily with Residence Life. It is crucial that an individual can relate well to others and handle administrative responsibilities. This position requires an individual who is flexible to assume a variety of roles and responsibilities. The duties and responsibilities for this position include the following. Developing an environment conducive to the academic, social, and personal success to each student Supervision of a diverse residential campus of students Supervision and training of RA staff Recruitment of RA staff Developing Educational/Social Programming in assigned area Monitor maintenance concerns Maintain accurate and up to date records of residents and files Active member of Student Services/Residence Life Team Maintain regular office hours in the Residence Life Department Assist in housing processes Participate in On-Call Schedule and Weekend Duty Capable of responding to various issues and emergency situations Participate and volunteer with various Residence Life/Student Services operational needs and services Some weekends may be required Other duties as assigned. Bachelor’s Degree is required, s ome experience may be substituted for educational requirements at the discretion of the hiring manager To apply, submit a letter of interest, recommendations and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. CUSTODIAN Posted: 8/28/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking an energetic individual to assume custodial duties. The selected applicant must enjoy working with young adults, faculty, and staff in a living/learning environment. To apply, please submit a letter of interest and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. DIRECTOR OF RESIDENCE LIFE Posted:  8/24/2026 The Director of Residence Life is a full-time, 12 month live-in position that oversees all Residential housing as well as all residential students. They supervise a staff of 7-8 Resident Hall Directors including Area Coordinators and 34-37 Resident Assistants. The Director of Residence Life collaborates with several other departments on campus to help ensure the safety of students as well as the conduct of all residential students and helps to make the residential experience conducive to a living and learning environment. The Director serves the interest of all residential students, ensures smooth operations, and guarantees quality customer service for all constituents (students, campus partners, prospective families, etc.). The duties and responsibilities for this position include the following. Oversees the daily operations of all Residential facilities including maintenance requests and the safety of the building Supervises a staff of Area Coordinators, Resident Directors, and Resident Assistants Creates an on call schedule for both Resident Directors and Resident Assistants Acts as the campus Sexual Assault Liaison and collaborates with the Title IX Coordinator as well as community partners to assist any student who may need those services. Oversees all conduct issues in collaboration with the Dean of Students’ office Collaborates with Admissions when housing incoming freshmen as well as oversees all of the housing for residential students Coordinates and oversees the training necessary for the College’s Professional Staff and the staff of Resident Assistants. Collaborates with Physical Plant Operations to ensure the cleanliness and maintenance of each Residential Hall, and places fines to student accounts when applicable. Collaborates with the Director of Student Activities regarding programs and activities during move-in weekend as well as throughout the year Responsible for reviewing and approving time-sheets for the Resident Directors Responsible for assignment and supervision of secondary duties for each Resident Director Collaborates with Resident Directors to provide guidance on any roommate conflicts Oversees all housing assignments for residential students as well any switch in housing assignments throughout the year Reports to the Dean of Students’ office Other duties as assigned. Bachelor’s Degree required, Master’s Degree in Higher Education, Administration, or related field strongly preferred, and a t least one year of experience in Higher Education To apply, submit a letter of interest, recommendations and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. APARTMENT MANAGER/STUDENT ACTIVITIES GRADUATE ASSISTANT Posted: 8/20/2026 This position serves as a live-in professional staff member with the Residence Life Department and Student Activities Department. Within Residence Life, this position focuses on enhancing the quality of life of students in the assigned apartment area, fostering community, being attentive to safety and security of residents and assisting with facility operations. Within Student Activities, this position will assist in planning, promoting, and managing a broad spectrum of campus activities and programs which will cultivate a vibrant/active social life and help to nurture student leadership and development This position will work daily with the Residence Life Department and the Student Activities Leadership team. It is crucial that an individual be able to relate well to others and handle administrative responsibilities. This position requires an individual who is flexible to assume a variety of roles and responsibilities. Residence Life responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Developing an environment conducive to the academic, social, and personal success for each student Supervision of a diverse residential campus of students Supervision and training of RA staff Monitor maintenance concerns Maintain accurate and up to date records of residents and files Active member of Student Services/Residence Life Team Maintain regular office hours in the Residence Life Department Assist in housing processes Participate in On-Call Schedule and Weekend Duty Capable of responding to various issues and emergency situations Participate and volunteer with various Residence Life/Student Services operational needs and services Some weekends required Other duties and responsibilities as assigned Graduate Assistant for Student Activities responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Coordinate and implement Student Activities programs Coordinate and implement Student Activities Board programs Create effective marketing strategies for programs and events sponsored by Student Activities Provide functional event support and management for all Student Activities and Student Activities Board events. Supervise the Cralle Student Union Building activity area(s) Supervise work-study employees assigned to activity area(s) Maintaining supplies and materials for the activity area(s) Some weekends may be required Other duties and responsibilities as assigned Bachelor's Degree is required, will consider application if Bachelor's Degree is not yet conferred Remuneration: Salary - $6000 stipend, 10-month part time contract Unfurnished apartment w/streaming service(s) and basic utilities included Meal plan (when cafeteria is open for meals) Graduate tuition up to 18hrs per year (tuition rate must not exceed LWU graduate program) Position is not eligible for health insurance or retirement program(s). To apply, submit a cover letter, recommendations and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. ASSISTANT ATHLETIC TRAINER Posted:  7/16/2026 Lindsey Wilson University, a private University located in Columbia KY, is seeking applicants for multiple Assistant Athletic Trainer positions within the Lindsey Wilson University Sports Medicine Department. These positions are full time over 11-months/year. The start date will be determined by the number of applicants and relocation. Lindsey Wilson University is a member of the Mid-South Conference and the National Association for Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and sponsors 28 varsity/club sports programs consisting of 36 teams and 800+ student-athletes. Position Title: Assistant Athletic Trainer Starting Salary: $50,000 with benefits (Additional assistance with relocation will be provided) Reports to: Head Athletic Trainer Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s or master’s in athletic training from a CAATE accredited University or university. Certification/Licenses: Must be Board of Certification (BOCATC) certified; Must be licensed or eligible for licensure through the Kentucky Medical Board of Licensure; Must be certified in ALS/BLS from the American Heart Association/American Red Cross. Additional Requirements: Must have a valid driver’s license and have a current NPI Number Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Applied Knowledge: Assistant athletic trainers must have knowledge of a large range of medical problems and conditions, including but not limited to: Orthopedic/Musculoskeletal, General Medical, Psychological, etc. Assessment and evaluation skills need to be proficient, with areas of growth to occur. Decision Making Skills: Assistant athletic trainers need to have the ability to think critically regarding assessment, treatment, rehabilitation, and return to play decisions, as per standing orders and state licensure guidelines. Attention to Detail: Assistant athletic trainers should be thorough and detailed in their injury documentation and tracking, along with their assessment and evaluation of athletic-related injuries and illnesses. Interpersonal Skills: Assistant athletic trainers must have the ability to communicate effectively in high stress/pressure situations when talking to student-athletes, medical professionals, staff and coaches. Organization: Assistant athletic trainers must have the ability to organize, prioritize, and perform multiple tasks with little to no supervision. Autonomy: Assistant athletic trainers need to be able to make independent decisions regarding assessments, treatments, rehabilitation and return to play. Assistant athletic trainers need to be able to work independently, with the cumulative support of the Sports Medicine department. Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Onsite care and management of injuries and illnesses including prevention, evaluation, management, and rehabilitation. Assess risk of injury, perform ergonomic evaluation and coaching, self-care implementation and overall wellness promotion. Coordinate and implement injury prevention programs and customized preventative strategies and program for each patient. Minimize risk of injury through awareness, education and prevention strategies. Provide accommodation recommendations, related to sport, for student-athletes with restrictions and/or limitation based upon clinician evaluation and assessments. Communicate with physicians and coaching staff regarding injury status of student-athletes. Responsible for administrative duties including electronic documentation for all patient encounters, filing and management of insurance claims and follow-ups, management and coordination of doctors/surgery appointments. Description of Athletics Program/Assignments: Lindsey Wilson University is a member of the Mid-South Conference and the National Association for Intercollegiate Athletics (NAIA) and sponsors 27 varsity/club sports programs consisting of 36 teams and 800+ student-athletes. Sporting assignments will be decided upon successful hiring and personal preferences. Sporting assignments could include: Football (2), Men’s and Women’s Soccer, XC and Track/Field, Men’s and Women’s Basketball, Cheerleading/Dance, Men’s and Women’s Swim, Softball, Men’s and Women’s Golf, Men’s and Women’s Bowling. Travel Responsibilities: Some travel may be required, based upon game coverage and athletic training room needs. Overnight travel may occur with conference games, and post-season/nationals travel as well. Physical Requirements: Lifting and carrying heavy objects. Medium strength is required to position student-athletes for examination. May assist student-athletes as needed, helping them on and off the exam table, or assisting athletes off the field for further evaluation. Ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings, weekends and holidays. Supervisory Responsibilities: Assistant athletic trainers will help supervise MSAT students and athletic training observation students, both within the athletic training room and at the sport practice/game sites. Additional Factors for Employment: Once selected, candidates will have to successfully complete a background check. Candidates must have a valid driver’s license. Lindsey Wilson University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Information to Apply: To apply, submit a cover letter, recommendations and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. WORDPRESS DEVELOPER INTERN Posted:  5/26/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking a motivated and creative WordPress Developer Intern to assist with the migration and redevelopment of the existing www.lindsey.edu website into WordPress. This internship position reports to the IT Department and works closely with the Public Relations to support website content, communications, and digital initiatives. This is an excellent opportunity for someone looking to gain hands-on experience working on a live educational website conversion project while building their portfolio and professional skills. Assist with converting the existing Lindsey.edu website to WordPress Develop, maintain, and improve WordPress pages, themes, and functionality Customize WordPress themes, plugins, and page layouts Collaborate regularly with the Public Relations Department during normal business hours to support website updates, branding, campaigns, and communications Integrate and work with third-party APIs and external data sources as needed Ensure website pages are visually appealing, responsive, and user-friendly Identify and troubleshoot website issues as needed Independently manage assigned tasks and meet project deadlines Support the IT Department in maintaining website functionality and performance Requirements Proficiency with WordPress website development and management Strong understanding of web design principles and user experience Good grasp of consuming and integrating APIs Working knowledge of HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and related web technologies Ability to meet and collaborate with Public Relations staff during standard business hours Self-motivated and capable of working independently Strong communication and organizational skills Portfolio or examples of previous WordPress/design work preferred What You'll Gain Real-world experience contributing to a large-scale website conversion project Opportunity to build and strengthen WordPress development, API integration, and design skills Experience working with both IT and Public Relations professionals Portfolio-building opportunities and professional references upon successful completion This is a non-paying internship position intended for individuals seeking practical experience in WordPress development, website design, API integration, and digital communications. To apply, please submit your resume along with any relevant portfolio links or examples of previous work through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. FLAG FOOTBALL GRADUATE ASSISTANT Posted:  5/7/2026 Lindsey Wilson University, located in Columbia, Kentucky, is seeking applicants for a Flag Football Graduate Assistant. Lindsey Wilson, a member of the Mid-South Conference and the NAIA, sponsors twenty-eight varsity athletic programs and has 800+ student-athletes participating in total. GA duties include, but are not limited to the following: conducting practices, weight training sessions, conditioning sessions, recruiting, monitoring academic progress of the student-athletes, fundraising, scheduling, and other coaching/administrative duties under direction of the head coach. Review of applications will begin immediately. A bachelor’s degree and valid driver’s license is required; previous collegiate playing and/or coaching experience preferred. The selected candidate will be provided a $5,000 stipend, graduate tuition at LWU (18 hours/year), on-campus housing and meals for their service. To apply, submit a cover letter, recommendations and resume through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Lindsey Wilson University is an EOE. ENROLLMENT COORDINATOR FOR EDUCATIONAL OUTREACH - LOUISVILLE CAMPUS Posted:  1/16/2026 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking applicants for an Enrollment Coordinator for our Louisville campus in Kentucky. This position is located on-site at our Louisville, KY campus. The coordinator is responsible for recruitment in Louisville/Lexington, Kentucky and surrounding areas throughout the region. Primary responsibilities include but are not limited to recruiting for all LWU programs, mentoring students throughout the admissions process, and functioning as a contact between the University, local agencies, and related educational institutions. Qualifications include: A bachelor’s degree, experience in marketing, networking, communication skills, and a valid driver’s license. The coordinator will demonstrate understanding of LWU’s philosophy of actively caring for students and providing excellent customer service to potential and enrolled students. Successful applicant must be reliable, trustworthy and able to successfully pass a background check. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, resume, and three references through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . The selection process will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity-focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day.” LWU strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. ADJUNCT FACULTY – EPIDEMIOLOGY Posted:  6/16/2025 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking a dynamic and experienced professional to join our Education Program as an Adjunct Instructor to teach Health Education courses online.  The successful candidate will bring both academic and practical expertise to educate and inspire the next generation of public health professionals. Job responsibilities include teaching undergraduate courses in Health Education, specifically, beginning with the EDUC Epidemiology course in fall of 2025, develop syllabi, lesson plans, and assessments in alignment with course objectives, engage students through interactive online lectures, discussions, and applied assignments, provide timely feedback and support to students, utilize the institution’s learning management system (LMS) Canvas for communication and grading and maintain availability for student questions and academic support A Master’s degree in Epidemiology, Public Health, or a related field is required, and a terminal degree is preferred.  Prior online or hybrid teaching experience at the college/university level is strongly preferred along with demonstrated expertise in health, epidemiological methods and data analysis. The position requires strong communication and organizational skills. Review of applications will begin immediately. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, curriculum vitae including names and contact information for three professional references, statement of teaching philosophy, unofficial copies of all graduate transcripts (official copies must be submitted prior to hiring) through the Lindsey Wilson University online employment application . Review of applicants will begin immediately and be ongoing until the position is filled. LWU is an equal opportunity employer committed to assembling a caring, equity focused faculty committed to supporting “every student, every day”. LWU strives to hire qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, age, disability, genetic information or status as a protected veteran. PART-TIME DINING CENTER SEASONAL WORKER Posted:  09/05/2023 Lindsey Wilson University is seeking applicants for the position of a generalized part time seasonal worker. A successful applicant must be highly organized and a self-starter. Responsibilities include general prepping, sanitation, dish washing and helping in other areas when needed. Send letter of interest and resume to: Human Resources, Lindsey Wilson University, 210 Lindsey Wilson Street, Columbia, Kentucky 42728, fax 270-384-7373 or e-mail hr@lindsey.edu or apply on-line at www.lindsey.edu. LWU is an EOE employer. APPLY NOW SCHEDULE A VISIT REQUEST INFORMATION Make a Gift Students, Faculty and Staff Cranmer Dining Center Holloway Health and Wellness Center Consumer Information Disclosure Cost of Attendance Library Bookstore LWU Online Accreditations LWU Licensure Disclosures Campus Map/Directions Directory Request a Transcript Employment Opportunities Students With Disabilities Teaching & Learning Commons COVID-19 Response Emergency Contacts Campus Nurse Public Safety Contact LWU Privacy Policy Every Student, Every Day L INDSEY W ILSON U NIVERSITY 210 Lindsey Wilson St. Columbia, KY 42728 Local: 270 384-2126  Fax: 270-384-8591  Toll Free: 800-264-0138  e-mail: info@lindsey.edu 210 Lindsey Wilson Street Columbia, Kentucky 42728 800-264-0138 • 270-384-2126 info@lindsey.edu www.lindsey.edu online.lindsey.edu www.lindseyathletics.com"
